        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-27T18:52:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like boringssl has some higher-level APIs to generate keys, such as [`EC_KEY_new_by_curve_name`](https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl/+/refs/heads/master/include/openssl/ec_key.h), which would simplify this code. Is the reason you\u0027re not using it because the TRNG isn\u0027t hooked up into boringssl?\n\nIt may be possible to make `boringssl`\u0027s rand use our TRNG with some hooks (we can ask the boringssl maintainers):\n\n* https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl/+/master/crypto/fipsmodule/rand/urandom.c#263\n\nIt looks like it\u0027s calling `getrandom()`, which we could implement (if it\u0027s not already in our `newlib` libc).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "c106608a85a501c669f5cfb01ad128fa3df98494",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
