      "writtenOn": "2023-04-27T18:15:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Pk\" is a bit ambiguous by itself. In this case it\u0027s meant to be \"pairing key\", but it could also be an abbreviation for \"private key\". Let\u0027s replace all instances of \"Pk\" with \"pairing_key\" in variable and function names to be clear.\n\nFor example:\n\n```\nFP_PAIRING_KEY_ENC_METADATA_VERSION\n```\n\n```\nec_response_fp_establish_pairing_key_keygen\n```\n\netc.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7743,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 7743,
        "endChar": 19
